From: Ryan Stoffel <stoffel.thomas.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:37:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] strip: skip the actions wisp leaves out

Some upstream features show up as an action rather than a view container
or a workbench contribution, which the registration filter already
covers. The Agents window's Copilot account button is one: its action
sits in the title bar at module load, and its contribution only draws
it, so excluding the contribution still leaves a text button behind.

The ids live in one wisp-owned list,
src/vs/platform/wisp/common/excludedActions.ts, which the overlay
provides. It sits in platform because registerAction2 does, and platform
code must not import from the workbench. registerAction2 returns before
registering an excluded action's command, menu entries, or keybinding.

diff --git a/src/vs/platform/actions/common/actions.ts b/src/vs/platform/actions/common/actions.ts
index 6ed9a9a6170392a04fbf75af8f9f2ec8996da98e..2ac60a3f54e261c7718ff7689b7245b95965e1a2 100644
--- a/src/vs/platform/actions/common/actions.ts
+++ b/src/vs/platform/actions/common/actions.ts
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ import { CommandsRegistry, ICommandService } from '../../commands/common/command
 import { ContextKeyExpr, ContextKeyExpression, IContextKeyService } from '../../contextkey/common/contextkey.js';
 import { createDecorator, ServicesAccessor } from '../../instantiation/common/instantiation.js';
 import { IKeybindingRule, KeybindingsRegistry } from '../../keybinding/common/keybindingsRegistry.js';
+import { isExcludedAction } from '../../wisp/common/excludedActions.js';
 
 export interface IMenuItem {
 	command: ICommandAction;
@@ -728,6 +729,9 @@ export abstract class Action2 {
 export function registerAction2(ctor: { new(): Action2 }): IDisposable {
 	const disposables: IDisposable[] = []; // not using `DisposableStore` to reduce startup perf cost
 	const action = new ctor();
+	if (isExcludedAction(action.desc.id)) {
+		return toDisposable(() => { });
+	}
 
 	const { f1, menu, keybinding, ...command } = action.desc;
 
